Jackass 3D (known as Jackass 3 on home media) is a 2010 American
3D reality comedy film directed by Jeff Tremaine.

12
00:49:02,608 --> 00:49:08,608
It is the third installment in the Jackass film series, and
the sequel to Jackass Number Two (2006).

13
00:53:07,826 --> 00:53:13,826
The film stars the regular Jackass cast of  Johnny Knoxville, Bam Margera, Ryan Dunn, Steve-O,
"Danger Ehren" McGhehey, Dave England, Preston Lacy, Wee Man, and Chris Pontius.

14
00:57:13,043 --> 00:57:19,043
This is the last Jackass film to feature Dunn before his death in 2011 and Margera as a primary
cast member before his departure in 2020 (Margera is briefly in Jackass Forever).

15
01:01:18,260 --> 01:01:24,260
It is also the last Jackass film to feature a guest
appearance by Rip Taylor, who died in October 2019.

16
01:05:23,478 --> 01:05:29,478
The film was theatrically released in the United States in the 3D format on October 15, 2010, by
Paramount Pictures, marking the tenth anniversary of the Jackass television series.

17
01:09:28,695 --> 01:09:34,695
It received generally positive reviews from critics.

18
01:13:33,913 --> 01:13:39,913
The film grossed $171.7 million worldwide against a
production budget of $20 million.

19
01:17:39,130 --> 01:17:45,130
A sequel, titled Jackass Forever, was released 12 years
later on February 4, 2022, to positive reviews.

20
